@jberryman , we are using the default batch size. Most of the cohorts are fairly full (50-100). The polling interval is 1/s.

<img width="1348" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9d531600-22c1-4a38-9012-dba616aff8a5" />

This is an example from AWS RDS Performance insights. This Hasura subscription query is our number 1 largest load in the system and is returning thousands and thousands of "empty" rows per second. I'm not sure if this number will actually go down by not returning the empty rows, but what I can say is that it would drop DB IO substantially and would eliminate a ton of CPU on Hasura spent just parsing empty json payloads.
